1
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:10,730
Hi everyone and welcome.

2
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:14,170
Let's start building our reading skills.

3
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:17,370
And here comes the very first lesson.

4
00:00:17,970 --> 00:00:19,770
I know that all of us can't wait

5
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:22,230
to take the exam right away and make

6
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:26,030
ourselves familiar with frequently asked questions in it.

7
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:31,650
However, it won't be useful unless our reading skills are improved.

8
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:34,530
And this is also the very first goal

9
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:38,230
that we need to achieve to master IELTS Reading.

10
00:00:39,810 --> 00:00:42,270
I want to start the lesson with a

11
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:44,010
small challenge for you guys.

12
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,590
On the next screen, there will be a picture.

13
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:49,190
You have 10 seconds to look at it

14
00:00:49,190 --> 00:00:52,710
and then answer some of my questions related to the picture.

15
00:00:53,170 --> 00:00:53,910
Are you ready?

16
00:00:54,570 --> 00:00:56,770
10 seconds starts now.

17
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:14,230
Okay, now let's answer my questions.

18
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:19,310
Number one, how many people are there in the picture?

19
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:22,350
Looking at the picture quickly, you can see

20
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:27,570
that there are three people, a man, a woman and a boy.

21
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:31,030
They look like a happy family, don't they?

22
00:01:31,470 --> 00:01:32,550
Let's continue.

23
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:36,770
Number two, is the car running?

24
00:01:37,370 --> 00:01:42,170
No, obviously the car stays still and even

25
00:01:42,170 --> 00:01:43,890
the trunk is still open.

26
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:46,970
We will answer one more question.

27
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:50,470
Number three, what's the mother doing?

28
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:53,350
She's holding her son's hand.

29
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:55,070
Good job, everyone.

30
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:56,370
Let's continue.

31
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:03,620
Now let's answer some more questions still about that picture.

32
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:08,110
Number one, how many trees are there in the picture?

33
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:10,950
Which brand of shoes is the woman wearing?

34
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:15,010
Number three, what is the type of the

35
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:16,290
house in the background?

36
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:18,970
I'm pretty sure that if you don't look

37
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:21,730
at the photo again, many of you can't

38
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:23,750
answer these three questions.

39
00:02:24,070 --> 00:02:26,310
Even if you look back at it, I'm

40
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:27,990
not sure you can answer them.

41
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:28,930
Just kidding.

42
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:31,510
You don't need to do that again to

43
00:02:31,510 --> 00:02:32,290
find the answer.

44
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:35,210
So why can you answer the first three

45
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:37,990
questions easily, but you can't do the same

46
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:40,250
thing with the three latter ones?

47
00:02:40,550 --> 00:02:43,670
Because the first three sentences show the main

48
00:02:43,670 --> 00:02:45,350
information of the picture.

49
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:48,190
They tell us what the picture is about.

50
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:52,510
In reading, these are called keywords, which are

51
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:56,570
really important pieces of information, helping us to

52
00:02:56,570 --> 00:02:59,930
understand the content of a sentence, a paragraph,

53
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:01,930
or a reading passage.

54
00:03:02,410 --> 00:03:05,430
The three latter questions are difficult to answer

55
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:09,410
because those are small details or minor details.

56
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:12,670
They do not affect the overall meaning.

57
00:03:13,350 --> 00:03:17,130
We can ignore them and still understand the main content.

58
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:21,580
When you read anything not only for IELTS Reading,

59
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:24,940
identifying and focusing on keywords,

60
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:28,610
ignoring minor details are necessary.

61
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:30,930
They help you to speed up the reading

62
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:33,690
process and get a lot of information in

63
00:03:33,690 --> 00:03:35,730
a short period of time.

64
00:03:36,270 --> 00:03:38,930
Our first lesson aims to help you.

65
00:03:39,570 --> 00:03:43,970
Number one, remember and understand the definition of keywords.

66
00:03:44,910 --> 00:03:49,050
Number two, understand different types of keywords.

67
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:53,410
And number three, apply the knowledge of keywords

68
00:03:53,410 --> 00:03:58,240
to the reading passage through three parts of the lesson.

69
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:01,300
Number one: Definition of keywords.

70
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:04,160
Number two: Types of keywords

71
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:11,140
And number three: Practice identifying keywords
in sentences and paragraphs.

72
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:15,320
Once you apply these core knowledge to IELTS Reading,

73
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,420
you will find it much easier.

74
00:04:17,610 --> 00:04:19,230
So stay with me.

75
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:21,590
All right, let's get started.

76
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:31,780
Keywords are words in a sentence, a passage,

77
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:34,840
a text, and carry the main content that

78
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,480
the writer wants to convey.

79
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:40,360
These words often have important meaning or serve

80
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:43,440
the purpose of placing emphasis based on the

81
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,800
writer's intention.

82
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:48,440
In other words, we just need to look at these words.

83
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,800
We still understand what the sentence is about.

84
00:04:52,340 --> 00:04:53,160
That's right.

85
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,520
Keywords help us narrow down the amount of

86
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:59,800
information we need to read and process questions

87
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,980
more quickly.

88
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:05,300
Human brains can only effectively process a certain

89
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:07,800
amount of information at a time.

90
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:11,920
Obviously, selecting what to read will make us

91
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:15,820
increase our reading speed, remember the information better,

92
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:20,360
and be more focused compared to reading all

93
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:24,020
the words in a sentence, a paragraph, or a text.

94
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:27,540
Now we've understood the definition, we're going to

95
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:30,360
learn about different types of keywords so that

96
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,040
we can use them effectively.

97
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,460
Let's go.

98
00:05:38,510 --> 00:05:40,470
To begin with, I would like to give

99
00:05:40,470 --> 00:05:41,770
you the following pictures.

100
00:05:42,610 --> 00:05:45,430
Please guess what I'm trying to talk about.

101
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:56,230
One thing in common between these pictures, as

102
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,750
you've already seen, is that they are cars.

103
00:06:00,090 --> 00:06:02,350
To be more specific, we are talking about

104
00:06:02,350 --> 00:06:04,070
different types of cars.

105
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:06,970
In the next screen, please pause the video

106
00:06:06,970 --> 00:06:10,830
and spend two minutes studying the highlighted keywords

107
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:13,950
in two colors in order to see the

108
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:15,170
differences between them.

109
00:06:15,770 --> 00:06:18,810
Once you have your own answers, we'll get

110
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:20,150
back to our lesson.

111
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:21,870
See you in a bit.

112
00:06:28,830 --> 00:06:31,550
I guess most of you notice that the

113
00:06:31,550 --> 00:06:35,850
yellow keywords are proper nouns or acronyms, don't you?

114
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:39,110
And the blue keywords are general words.

115
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:44,420
In general, the yellow keywords are called unchangeable keywords

116
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:47,210
or keywords that cannot be changed.

117
00:06:47,570 --> 00:06:48,910
Sounds reasonable, right?

118
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:52,770
Since it's a personal name, we cannot change anything.

119
00:06:53,590 --> 00:06:56,700
The blue keywords are changeable keywords

120
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:59,190
or the keywords that can be changed.

121
00:06:59,650 --> 00:07:03,390
In this example, types can be replaced by kinds.

122
00:07:03,790 --> 00:07:07,670
They both refer to a particular group of something.

123
00:07:08,310 --> 00:07:11,550
Big can be replaced to large.

124
00:07:12,410 --> 00:07:14,970
Good can be replaced with suitable.

125
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:18,950
Trips can be replaced with journeys.

126
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:22,100
They have the same meaning.

127
00:07:22,670 --> 00:07:25,590
In this context, taken off is used when

128
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:27,970
we are talking about a car with a

129
00:07:27,970 --> 00:07:28,890
removable roof.

130
00:07:29,330 --> 00:07:32,090
So, we can replace it with removed.

131
00:07:32,810 --> 00:07:35,950
Very can be replaced with extremely.

132
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:39,550
Fun can be replaced with exciting.

133
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:45,250
And the phrase run on means using electricity to run.

134
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:48,930
Instead, we can change it to the word use.

135
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:54,380
Let's get more specific about each type, shall we?

136
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:57,600
Starting with changeable keywords.

137
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,140
We're going to look at all the changeable

138
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:02,640
keywords we just saw in the last example

139
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:04,200
one more time.

140
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,480
Now, I'd like you to name the part

141
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:10,540
of speech of those keywords and divide them

142
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:12,720
into four groups for me.

143
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:16,920
Let's spend about one minute doing this exercise.

144
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,680
Make it fast, everyone.

145
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:22,120
Three, two, one, start.

146
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:28,820
These keywords are divided into four groups corresponding

147
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:31,200
to four parts of speech.

148
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,760
Nouns.

149
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:34,780
Types.

150
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:36,420
Trips.

151
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:38,600
Verbs.

152
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:40,880
Taken off.

153
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:43,420
Run on.

154
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,140
Adjectives.

155
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:47,820
Big.

156
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:49,840
Good.

157
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:51,780
Fun.

158
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,280
Adverbs.

159
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:55,800
Very.

160
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:00,200
That's right.

161
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:05,260
When we read a sentence, nouns, verbs, adjectives,

162
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:08,140
adverbs are the words we need to focus

163
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:11,420
on because they will often be the keywords

164
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:15,440
expressing the main content of the sentence.

165
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:18,780
There are other parts of speech like pronouns,

166
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,720
prepositions, or articles.

167
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:24,640
We can skip them and still understand the meaning.

168
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:29,980
Now, let's come to unchangeable keywords or keywords

169
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:32,140
that cannot be changed.

170
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:37,320
There are three common types of unchangeable keywords

171
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,760
including proper nouns.

172
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:42,620
The main feature of these words is to

173
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:44,680
capitalize the first letters.

174
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:49,280
Names of people, places, companies, and brands are

175
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:52,480
often in this group and these keywords are

176
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:56,720
really easy to find because of their capital letters.

177
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:01,180
In our example, there are the names of two cars.

178
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:05,640
Kia Sorento and Mercedes-Benz GT.

179
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,000
Acronyms.

180
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:12,480
Acronyms like the word SUV in the paragraph

181
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,200
introducing the cars.

182
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:18,640
This is an acronym for Sport Utility Vehicle

183
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:21,460
or our word IELTS.

184
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,220
It's also an acronym.

185
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:28,580
The full phrase is International English Language Testing System.

186
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:32,040
Well, it is just hard to remember,

187
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:34,620
so you just have to say IELTS.

188
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,020
But remember to pronounce it right.

189
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,640
Do not pronounce it like IELT.

190
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:43,330
While the nouns we only capitalize the first

191
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:47,330
letters, with acronyms we usually capitalize all the

192
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:50,390
letters which make them easier to identify.

193
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,430
This is also a type of keyword we

194
00:10:53,430 --> 00:10:55,190
need to pay attention to.

195
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,000
Numbers.

196
00:10:58,660 --> 00:11:03,280
Numbers are often categorized as unchangeable keywords due

197
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:08,300
to their nature of expressing specific quantities which

198
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:09,760
are rarely changed.

199
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:15,480
We can find metrics, time, and currencies in this group.

200
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:20,600
For example, there are about 26 types of cars available.

201
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:23,200
No kidding, that's a lot.

202
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:27,260
Until now, the knowledge is quite enough so

203
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,620
let's practice.

204
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:29,840
Here we go.

205
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:37,060
Let's start with something simple.

206
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,660
In the first exercise, your task is very simple.

207
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,800
I have some keywords available for you here.

208
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:48,320
Within 30 seconds, please divide them into two groups.

209
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,620
Changeable keywords and unchangeable keywords.

210
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,000
That's all.

211
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:54,960
Are you ready?

212
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,880
In three, two, one, go.

213
00:11:58,620 --> 00:11:59,760
Here's the key.

214
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,880
Let's check together.

215
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:09,020
This exercise is just a warm-up activity.

216
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,980
It has nothing challenging at all.

217
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:15,460
Now we're going to make it a bit more difficult.

218
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:17,360
I'll give you some sentences.

219
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:21,060
Please identify the keywords in each sentence and

220
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:21,980
categorize them.

221
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,460
You are going to pause the video on

222
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,620
the next screen to do this task within

223
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:31,100
one minute and then we'll check the answers together.

224
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:32,140
Let's do it everyone.

225
00:12:37,510 --> 00:12:39,550
All right, here's the key.

226
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:42,770
If there is any new vocab, remember to

227
00:12:42,770 --> 00:12:45,030
write them down in your notebook.

228
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:53,080
Let's finish with the most challenging task.

229
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:54,940
Now, I'll give you a passage.

230
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:58,220
Help me point out the keywords and categorize them.

231
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,440
Let's spend about five minutes doing this.

232
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,700
Pause the video so that you can do

233
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,480
it carefully and then check the answer.

234
00:13:12,990 --> 00:13:14,330
Here's the answer.

235
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:15,970
Let's check together.

236
00:13:21,590 --> 00:13:24,990
After this exercise, you will probably wonder why

237
00:13:24,990 --> 00:13:30,010
all nouns, verbs, adjectives and adverbs are not

238
00:13:30,010 --> 00:13:31,750
highlighted as keywords.

239
00:13:32,230 --> 00:13:34,290
I'm going to give you two tips on

240
00:13:34,290 --> 00:13:37,470
identifying keywords so that you can narrow down

241
00:13:37,470 --> 00:13:39,750
the amount of information you have to read

242
00:13:39,750 --> 00:13:43,270
and increase your reading speed.

243
00:13:44,470 --> 00:13:47,650
The words which are mentioned several times only

244
00:13:47,650 --> 00:13:49,730
need to be identified once.

245
00:13:50,450 --> 00:13:52,560
For example, in the last reading,

246
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:57,580
two words "brands" and "cars" appear continuously,

247
00:13:57,580 --> 00:14:00,700
so identifying them in the first sentence is enough.

248
00:14:00,870 --> 00:14:03,510
We can skip them in the remaining sentences.

249
00:14:04,470 --> 00:14:08,470
Words with general meanings used for many contexts

250
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:12,230
can be omitted, even though they belong to

251
00:14:12,230 --> 00:14:15,850
the noun, verb, adjective or adverb group.

252
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:25,970
For example, to be, have, include, they're, and people, etc.

253
00:14:26,810 --> 00:14:32,000
By that, we can leave out more information that needs attention.

254
00:14:32,450 --> 00:14:35,850
Please note them down so you can practice more.

255
00:14:40,810 --> 00:14:42,290
Well done, everyone!

256
00:14:42,830 --> 00:14:45,610
We've completed the first skill building lesson of

257
00:14:45,610 --> 00:14:48,490
the Reading 4.0 - 5.0 course, which focuses

258
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:50,600
on identifying keywords,

259
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:55,140
categorizing changeable keywords and unchangeable keywords.

260
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:58,330
Also, we've achieved three goals.

261
00:14:59,070 --> 00:15:04,710
The first is remember and understand the definition of keywords.

262
00:15:05,310 --> 00:15:08,690
The second, understand different types of keywords.

263
00:15:09,490 --> 00:15:12,510
And the third, apply the knowledge of keywords

264
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:14,390
to the reading passage.

265
00:15:15,190 --> 00:15:17,630
See you all in the next lesson.

266
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:19,910
I'm Teacher Francois.

267
00:15:20,570 --> 00:15:21,380
Goodbye.

